  "guideEndTitle": "01  ·  Set up the End View",
  "guideEndBody": "Use one quill. Make the outer boundary visible, avoid shadows and put the ArUco marker beside the end in the same plane. A marker by itself is not a valid sample.",
  "guideSideTitle": "02  ·  Observe the surface",
  "guideSideBody": "Photograph the same quill from the side. Look for visible cracks, damage, uneven rolling and surface irregularities. A finishing model must use classes from the real dataset.",
  "guideMeasureTitle": "03  ·  Understand the measurements",
  "guideMeasureBody": "Maximum Feret diameter measures the greatest boundary-to-boundary distance. Minimum Feret width is the smallest supporting-line separation. Equivalent diameter comes from area. Circumference follows the actual outer contour.",
